{"id": "EUVD-2026-86248", "enisaUuid": "155f787a-8b6a-3458-812d-d69c8a1b096b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Fix response queue over-consumption in __qla_consume_iocb()\n\nqla24xx_process_response_queue() advances ring_ptr past the head IOCB\nbefore dispatching, so by the time __qla_consume_iocb() runs, ring_ptr\nalready points at the first continuation IOCB. The function however\nlooped purex->entry_count times starting at ring_ptr. As entry_count\nincludes the head, this consumed one entry too many: it stamped\nRESPONSE_PROCESSED on the next, unrelated IOCB and advanced the ring\npast it, silently dropping a legitimate firmware response. The head\nIOCB's signature was also never marked.\n\nMark the head processed and account for it, then consume only the\nentry_count - 1 continuation IOCBs, matching __qla_copy_purex_to_buffer().", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:40:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:07:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a136c311676fd1010b1bde3bcfd410caa2fa040f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d841707fafba5f80341b82e8c3a4c24fc5aa5132", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e3f129538c32d0019437197735912308c161843", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd1534d4afab47f13dfc27fff6f59dd859a0ac3a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31715d1e1cbf3a37ce3452635c5602f73fd7abd4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df86c27cf1ba9d66f737a1fa56479c6e7efafe4e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ba019bdd89d931499d9476456b5d9c7ab7fa753"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93242", "GHSA-w8h6-pxw4-jqxh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f083d8c-1ebe-3810-81e3-5db878e593b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fac2807946c10b9a509b9c348afd442fa823c5f7 <a136c311676fd1010b1bde3bcfd410caa2fa040f"}, {"id": "1ffd5c67-3465-3fa6-a142-01dd965952d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_vers